    },
    "CardDescription": {
        "ParentObjectID": "fl_sunken_lake",
        "LocalizationKey": "Forest_Lore_CaveLake_CardDescription",
        "DefaultText": "A still black lake fills the floor of the cave, cold and clear, with a shelf of pale stone along one edge to kneel on. It never skins over and never floods, whatever the weather is doing above. You can drink from it, fill a container, wash in it, and fish or spear for eels and crayfish. Only a few eels live here: fish them out and the lake gives up about one a day. Like any pond's, the water is not safe to drink."
    },
